    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d338-a1">

                <pb facs="0615" n="521" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg521"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Marquis of Lansdowne to Sir Henry
                    Holland.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Government House</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Ottawa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1887-04-12"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 12,
                    1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I caused to he referred for the
                    consideration of my government a copy of your dispatch of the 23d February last
                    transmitting copy of a letter from the foreign office, with its inclosures,
                    respecting the case of the <hi rendition="#italic">Sarah H. Prior</hi> and
                    requesting to be furnished with a report upon the alleged conduct of the captain
                    of the Canadian revenue <pb facs="0616" n="522" xml:id="pg522"/> critter <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Critic</hi> on the occasion referred to, and I have now
                    the honor to forward herewith a certified copy of an approved report of a
                    committee of my privy council embodying a statement of Captain McLaren, of the
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Critic</hi>, with reference to the circumstances
                    complained of.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansdowne.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
